WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.382
Subscribers must plan for duplicates, failures and
delayed delivery.

00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:10.568
An idempotent handler prevents repeated execution
from creating an extra effect, but it does not

00:00:10.568 --> 00:00:12.566
make out-of-order changes safe.

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:18.752
Include entity versions or process related events in
an ordered partition when sequence matters.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:25.067
A priority queue changes which message runs first;
it is not a substitute for preserving business-

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:25.840
event order.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.632
The robotics example organizes computation into
nodes with typed messages.

00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:36.913
Topics carry streams such as sensor readings,
services provide request-and-response interactions,

00:00:36.913 --> 00:00:41.186
and actions support longer goals with progress and a
final result.

00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:47.338
These interfaces let sensing, planning, control and
visualization evolve separately while still

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:53.813
communicating through explicit data contracts suited
to their interaction patterns and timing needs.
